abstract = {From the perspective of body aesthetic education theory, this study proposes an algorithm-driven and system-integrated technical framework tailored for immersive design in university cultural venues. By establishing quantitative metrics such as interaction latency models and sensory synergy indices, the framework transforms physical engagement, multimodal perception, and aesthetic generation into computable and optimizable technical parameters. This architecture provides actionable technical solutions for transitioning university cultural venues from “visual displays” to “body-driven” aesthetic education paradigms. Future research will further explore real-time scenario generation technologies based on generative AI, conduct large-scale, long-term quantitative evaluations, and advance immersive design to effectively support body aesthetic education and comprehensive educational objectives.},
